<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Android Auto Backup rules for Salah (API 30 and below; see data_extraction_rules.xml for 31+).

  What is backed up, and why it is exactly this:

    file/datastore        Salah's preferences and the saved location. These are stored with
                          androidx.datastore.preferences, which writes a single file to
                          `<filesDir>/datastore/<name>.preferences_pb`. The `file` domain is
                          therefore the domain that actually contains them — the previous
                          configuration named only `sharedpref`, which Salah does not use, so the
                          intent ("the theme and the manual location are small and safe to back up")
                          was not being carried out and a device transfer silently lost both.

    sharedpref            Kept because it costs nothing and is the right domain if any dependency
                          ever stores a preference the platform way.

  What is deliberately NOT backed up:

    file/datasets         An applied dataset payload (see LocalDatasetStore). It is replaceable
                          data that can be produced again from a publication, it can be large, and
                          restoring a stale copy over a newer one would be worse than restoring
                          nothing. The bundled assets inside the APK always reconstruct a usable
                          dataset, so excluding it loses no capability.

  Because only <include> entries are listed, everything else is excluded — the dataset payloads
  above do not need an explicit <exclude>. If an <exclude> is ever added here, one is needed for
  `file/datasets` too, because an <exclude> would otherwise widen what is captured.
-->
<full-backup-content>
    <include domain="file" path="datastore/" />
    <include domain="sharedpref" path="." />
</full-backup-content>
